# Built frontend artifacts are bytes, not source.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true (the default on the Windows development machine) git
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout for anything it considers text. That changes
# the file's SHA-256 without changing a single line of code, so
# scripts/verify_git_prod_sync.py compared a CRLF working-tree bundle against
# the LF bundle production serves and reported drift on a deploy that was in
# fact byte-identical. Marking these paths binary keeps the checked-out bytes
# equal to the committed bytes on every platform.
static/assets/** -text
static/index.html -text
static/production.manifest.json -text
